  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A typical, family-run beach restaurant, "the last typical cabin on Pampelonne" below the Camarat lighthouse, Le Migon sits right at the far end of the beach. Provençal cuisine (seafood platter, clam pasta, a generous octopus salad), a terrace facing the sea in summer and a fireplace to warm up by in winter: it's one of the few places in the area open all year round. Dogs are allowed, confirmed by past customers who brought their companion along. The reviews are excellent and consistent across two platforms: 4.6/5 (732 reviews) and 4.8/5 on Restaurant Guru (2,317 reviews).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Open all year, every day — but closing times differ depending on the source: the official website states 8am-midnight, our previous listing stated 11:30pm, and one aggregator mentions tighter winter hours (9am-5pm then 5pm-9:30pm Friday/Saturday/Sunday only). It's best to check the day's hours directly on the official website (le-migon-restaurant-ramatuelle.fr) before travelling out of season. Free parking, boat shuttles and wifi are handy extras for planning your day on Pampelonne.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: out of season, the terrace with the fireplace is a good option for a quiet lunch facing the sea, without the summer crowds.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>You're on the Plage de Pampelonne, a few minutes from Saint-Tropez: perfect for combining the beach with your dog and a walk around the village.</p>
